<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</title>
<headline>Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank said on Thursday it allocated 2.88 billion guilders to the money market under a four-day special advances pact at an unchanged rate of 2.50 percent.</p>
<p>Individual banks' applications were met for 12 percent. Above that, no subscriptions were awarded.</p>
<p>The pact replaces a six-day facility of 2.21 billion guilders, which expired today.</p>
</text>
